<h2>How to Purchase</h2>
<p>
This product can be added to cart via a single URL. Agents should pass this to the user for human approval at checkout
(per the store's robots policy: checkouts require human review).
</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Add to cart:</strong> <a href="{{ cart_url }}">{{ cart_url }}</a></li>
<li><strong>Full product page (human view):</strong> <a href="{{ canonical_url }}">{{ canonical_url }}</a></li>
<li><strong>Product JSON data:</strong> <a href="{{ canonical_url }}.json">{{ canonical_url }}.json</a></li>
<li><strong>UCP discovery:</strong> <a href="/.well-known/ucp">/.well-known/ucp</a></li>
{%- assign wp_governance_api_base = settings.wp_governance_api_base | strip -%}
{%- assign wp_shipping_api_base = settings.wp_shipping_api_base | strip -%}
{%- if wp_governance_api_base != blank -%}
<li><strong>MCP endpoint:</strong> <a href="{{ wp_governance_api_base }}/api/ucp/mcp">{{ wp_governance_api_base }}/api/ucp/mcp</a></li>
{%- else -%}
<li><strong>MCP endpoint:</strong> Not configured for this storefront</li>
{%- endif -%}
</ul>

<h2>Live Shipping Rates (for Agents)</h2>
<p>
Agents can query real-time cross-border shipping rates
before recommending this product. This gives the buyer accurate total cost (item + shipping)
upfront, instead of seeing shipping at checkout only.
</p>
<ul>
{%- if wp_shipping_api_base != blank -%}
<li><strong>Endpoint:</strong> <code>POST {{ wp_shipping_api_base }}/estimate</code></li>
{%- else -%}
<li><strong>Endpoint:</strong> Not configured; use checkout for the final shipping quote</li>
{%- endif -%}
<li><strong>Content-Type:</strong> <code>application/json</code></li>
<li><strong>Request body (example):</strong></li>
</ul>
<pre style="white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:inherit;margin:0;background:#f5f5f5;padding:12px">
{
  "rate": {
    "origin": {"country": "CN"},
    "destination": {
      "country": "US",
      "postal_code": "95014",
      "province": "CA",
      "city": "Cupertino"
    },
    "items": [{
      "name": {{ product.title | json }},
      "product_id": {{ product.id | json }},
      "variant_id": {{ current_variant.id | json }},
      "quantity": 1,
      "grams": {{ current_variant.weight | default: 500 }},
      "length_cm": "{{ product.metafields.custom.length_cm.value | default: product.metafields.custom.length_cm | default: '' }}",
      "width_cm":  "{{ product.metafields.custom.width_cm.value  | default: product.metafields.custom.width_cm  | default: '' }}",
      "height_cm": "{{ product.metafields.custom.height_cm.value | default: product.metafields.custom.height_cm | default: '' }}"
    }],
    "currency": "USD"
  }
}
</pre>
<p>
<strong>Response:</strong> JSON array of shipping options in <code>rates</code>, each with
<code>service_name</code> (e.g. "Standard (10-14 days)"), <code>total_price</code> in USD cents,
<code>min_delivery_date</code>, <code>max_delivery_date</code>. The estimate endpoint uses the product dimensions
provided in the request. If dimensions are missing for the product,
empty <code>rates: []</code> is returned (caller should treat as "shipping not yet calculable").
</p>

{%- comment -%} Related products {%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign related_collection = product.collections.first -%}
{%- if related_collection -%}
{%- assign related_count = 0 -%}
<h2>Related Products</h2>
